{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/1809","id":1753440761,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz885og2H5","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1809","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1809.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1809.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/1809","number":1809,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"update gh workflow actions","user":{"login":"vdovhanych","id":45185420,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MTg1NDIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45185420?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vdovhanych","html_url":"https://github.com/vdovhanych","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vdovhanych/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vdovhanych/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vdovhanych/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vdovhanych/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vdovhanych/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vdovhanych/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vdovhanych/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vdovhanych/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vdovhanych/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nHeadscale is \"Open Source, acknowledged contribution\", this means that any\r\ncontribution will have to be discussed with the Maintainers before being submitted.\r\n\r\nThis model has been chosen to reduce the risk of burnout by limiting the\r\nmaintenance overhead of reviewing and validating third-party code.\r\n\r\nHeadscale is open to code contributions for bug fixes without discussion.\r\n\r\nIf you find mistakes in the documentation, please submit a fix to the documentation.\r\n-->\r\n\r\nWhat is changed by this PR:\r\n\r\n- Updates the various actions used for the projects workflows\r\n- Changes the `tj-actions/changed-files` to better maintained action `dorny/paths-filter` usage is basically the same and from what i tested its working as expected.\r\n\t- This also allows a better granularity for the file filters with more options to conditionally run what is needed. \r\n\t```yaml\r\n      - name: Get changed files\r\n        id: changed-files\r\n        uses: dorny/paths-filter@v3\r\n        with:\r\n          filters: |\r\n            yaml-files:\r\n              - 'config-example.yaml'\r\n            go-files\r\n              - '**/*.go'\r\n            nix-files\r\n              - '*.nix'\r\n\t```\r\n\tand the you can use it with `steps.changed-files.outputs.<filter-name> == 'true'` to run it only if the files from that filter were changed.\r\n- Small adjustments to file formatting\r\n\r\nAs next step i would like to introduce some naming conventions for the action files, workflow names and so on. But this is more upt to you guys if youd like that change.\r\n\r\n<!-- Please tick if the following things apply. You… -->\r\n\r\n- [x] read the [CONTRIBUTING guidelines](README.md#contributing)\r\n- [ ] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\r\n- [ ] added unit tests\r\n- [ ] added integration tests\r\n- [ ] updated documentation if needed\r\n- [ ] updated CHANGELOG.md\r\n\r\n<!-- If applicable, please reference the issue using `Fixes #XXX` and add tests to cover your new code. -->\r\n","created_at":"2024-03-03T15:02:53Z","updated_at":"2024-03-13T12:43:06Z","closed_at":"2024-03-13T12:43:06Z","merged_at":"2024-03-13T12:43:06Z","merge_commit_sha":"ef26f5808549b4a1d59d0b7e5f628633bcb16330","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/1809/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/1809/comments","review_co